  "rich_explanations": {
    "nahw": "Naḥw — what this piece does here: The body سُفَهَاء is the explicit subject of آمَنَ in the كما clause. Therefore the final ḍammah ُ is the visible nominative ending; it is separated from the lexical body.",
    "sarf": "Ṣarf — how this piece forms the word: The root س ف ه is retained. The singular سَفِيه follows فَعِيل; the plural body سُفَهَاء follows فُعَلَاء. The paired certified augment inventories name ي for the singular and ا + ء for the plural, so the plural has no ي."
  },
